  "dg.proptrees.chunks": "4 pointers: (t_node, c_node, e_node, s_node)",
  "ch5.p3": "Every vector chunk emitted later in Paint simply stores a compact 4-tuple pointing to one node in each tree: <code>(t_node, c_node, e_node, s_node)</code>. Once committed to <code>cc</code>, compositor scrolls mutate the Scroll/Transform node directly, and compositor animations update Transform or Effect nodes in place—Blink's main-thread Style, Layout, and Paint stay completely idle.",
  "ch5.model.title": "Model 4 · Four Property Trees mutator",
  "ch5.model.how": "Choose which property updates (transform / scroll / opacity / left), drag translation, scroll, and alpha sliders, and watch which single Property Tree turns dirty on the left while the clipped viewport updates on the right.",
